From 29a377c8411d8575070606caa005378c8cf54c3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alex <49746433+Master-Yoba@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 23:14:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ss-delta: keyboard and gamepad bindings in ss-delta.ini;
 keyboard input on the SDL frontend

Only the Qt interface turned keys into Vita buttons, so ss-delta.exe could
be played with a gamepad only. ss-delta now does it for SDL key events,
as the Qt keyboard filter does, and releases everything when the window
loses focus.

[keyboard] binds each Vita button (and the two sticks' directions) to up
to two keys: W3C codes, single letters or digits, or SDL-style names (Up,
Return, Left Shift, Keypad 1). [gamepad] binds a Vita button to one SDL
gamepad button through Vita3K's controller_binds. Unusable lines are
logged and leave the default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
